;
; TEXTEDIT with the alias ED: Enter keeps the value, Undo ([0.8.1-RT11], work #939;
; card PT11, point 2; ADR 0054, point 6).
; - An empty line at "Enter new text <value>:" is Enter (ConfirmInput): the TEXT keeps
;   its value and there is no Textedit step (card PT11, point 2).
; - Undo cancels the last modification of the command (the MTEXT, back to "Beta") and
;   writes "The command has been completely undone."; a second Undo, with nothing
;   left to undo in the command, writes the same message (session of 2026-11-22).
; - In a second ED, Undo before any modification writes the message and leaves the
;   modification of the first ED ("Delta") in place; Enter keeps "Beta".
; ~box of "Delta": Liberation Sans 2.1.5 advances read with fontTools (D 1479,
; e 1139, l 455, t 569, a 1139: 4781 font units), cap height 1409, ascent 1854,
; descent -434: width 4781 / 1409 * 2.5 = 8.482966643009227.
TEXT
0,0
2.5
0
Alfa

MTEXT
0,-10
60,-20
Beta

ED
1,1

1,-11
Gamma
U
U
1,1
Delta

!report
ED
U
1,-11


